§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–But king Solomon loved many strange women, together with the daughter of Pharaoh, women of the Moabites, Ammonites, Edomites, Zidonians, and Hittites;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙéof the nations concerning which the LORD said unto the children of Israel, Ye shall not go in to them, neither shall they come in unto you: for surely they will turn away your heart after their gods: Solomon clave unto these in love.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnAnd he had seven hundred wives, princesses, and three hundred concubines: and his wives turned away his heart.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼For it came to pass, when Solomon was old, that his wives turned away his heart after other gods: and his heart was not perfect with the LORD his God, as was the heart of David his father.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqFor Solomon went after Ashtoreth the goddess of the Zidonians, and after Milcom the abomination of the Ammonites.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd Solomon did evil in the sight of the LORD, and went not fully after the LORD, as did David his father.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªThen did Solomon build an high place for Chemosh, the abomination of Moab, in the hill that is before Jerusalem, and for Molech, the abomination of the children of Ammon.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd likewise did he for all his strange wives, which burnt incense and sacrificed unto their gods.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book
